window.TROPHIES=[{"id":"vice-got-a-price","grade":"platinum","name":"Vice Got a Price!","description":"Congratulations! You're a Leonida Legend.","guide":"Pops automatically once the other fifty-four trophies are done, so treat this as a progress check rather than a goal of its own. Every requirement is single-player and available offline: there are no online, DLC or difficulty-settings trophies, and one playthrough is enough. The only real gate is Completionist's 100% checklist under Progress > Stats > 100% Completion, which is far gentler than it sounds and asks for only about sixty percent of the game's actual content. Work the six roadmap stages in order, keep a manual save at the start and end of every chapter, and remember the single true missable is the Chapter 1 balcony meditation for Positive Mental Attitude. Expect roughly two hundred hours from start to platinum.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":6,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"leonida-legend","grade":"gold","name":"Leonida Legend","description":"Earn every trophy in Grand Theft Auto VI.","guide":"Unlocks when the other fifty-four trophies are all earned. Nothing here is online or DLC-gated, so a single offline save file is all you need. There is no New Game+ and no mission replay, which is why you should rotate the fifteen manual save slots and hold one at the start and end of each chapter plus a few for free-roam cleanup. The long tail is the 100% Completion checklist, not the story, and the only trophy you can permanently miss is Positive Mental Attitude's Chapter 1 meditation. Follow the six stages top to bottom and the checklist's lenient thresholds, 200 of 277 vehicle scans, 100 of 255 animal studies and 70 of 80 challenges, do most of the lifting.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":6,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"mastermind","grade":"gold","name":"Mastermind","description":"Complete every heist without failing.","guide":"Heists are the story set-pieces, headlined by The Cartel Heist in Chapter 3, and without failing means clearing each with no deaths and no failed objective that forces a checkpoint restart. The game autosaves aggressively, so if anything goes wrong pause and load the most recent checkpoint before the failure registers. Keep a manual save right before each heist so you can retry cleanly. Bank jobs and the eight large-bank vaults that feed Completionist also count as heists: after Chapter 3's Credit Check you get the Dye Pack Jammer, which lets you fence marked bills. Scout the escape route before you start and carry body armor, because a vault always draws a four-star wanted level you have to shake.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://gta.wiki/w/Achievements_and_Trophies_in_GTA_VI","title":"Achievements and Trophies in Grand Theft Auto VI","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"completionist","grade":"silver","name":"Completionist","description":"Reach 100% completion.","guide":"Reach 100% via the checklist at Progress > Stats > 100% Completion. It only appears after the credits, but everything you did before then already counts, and nothing on it is missable. You do not need everything: roughly 200 of 277 base-model vehicle scans with the WAiNK app, 100 of 255 animal studies through binoculars, 70 of 80 challenges, 300 of 397 stunts, 15 of 18 meditation spots and 100 optional tasks. The few things you must finish in full are the 39 gang operations, 22 bank jobs, 42 shooting-range gold medals, 42 drone races, 33 underwater discoveries and Bret's 15 Target Decks. Tick the list off against PowerPyx's checklist as you go and it will come together without a grind.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":6,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"survivor","grade":"silver","name":"Survivor","description":"Survive 5 stars for 10 minutes.","guide":"Get a five-star wanted level and stay alive for ten real minutes, then escape. The easy way is to grab a fast armored vehicle or steal a Rhino tank from Mile Zero Air Station in Mariana County, drive into a tunnel or under a highway where helicopters cannot shoot you, and keep moving so cops never surround you. The timer only cares about survival, so you can also hole up somewhere with hard cover and pick off pursuers. Do not enter any cheat code, since cheats disable trophies and saving outright. When the trophy pops, break line of sight, swap vehicles to drop the heat, and wait for the stars to clear.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":5,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"speedrunner","grade":"silver","name":"Speedrunner","description":"Complete the story in under 30 hours.","guide":"The story normally takes sixty to eighty hours, so finishing it in under thirty means skipping almost everything optional. Rush the pink main-story icons only, ignore the black-and-pink optional tasks and collectibles, use fast travel whenever it is offered, and skip every cutscene. Do this on its own save so your relaxed completion run stays intact, or stack it onto a second playthrough after the platinum is otherwise done. Stock up on body armor and buy a fast car early to shorten travel time. You will lock yourself out of nothing, but the Chapter 1 meditation is still missable, so grab it even on a fast run.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"pacifist","grade":"silver","name":"Pacifist","description":"Complete a mission without killing anyone.","guide":"Complete a single mission without killing anyone. The opening Chapter 1 missions are the safest: Gone Fishing is a tutorial with no forced combat, so simply avoid shooting and avoid takedowns that count as lethal. If a mission does put you in a fight, use non-lethal knockdowns where available or keep to cover and let scripted allies do the shooting. Stealth past guards with the Snap Gun once you unlock it in Chapter 3. Watch the kill counter on the results screen if one is shown, and if you accidentally drop someone, reload the checkpoint immediately. A clean early mission is far less fiddly than a late-game one.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"ghost","grade":"silver","name":"Ghost","description":"Complete a mission undetected.","guide":"Complete one mission fully undetected, meaning no alarms raised and no enemy spots you. Pick a stealth-capable mission: once Chapter 3's Yasmani's Jewelry Jobs unlocks the Snap Gun, you can silently lockpick a jewelry store's back door and rob it without tripping the alarm. Crouch, stick to cover, watch the detection meters, and disable cameras rather than sprinting past them. Plan the route before you move so guards never turn toward you. If you are spotted, pause and reload rather than fighting on, since a single alert voids the run. The backdoor approach beats the front-door smash every time.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"perfectionist","grade":"silver","name":"Perfectionist","description":"Complete every mission with a gold medal.","guide":"Every mission needs a gold medal, so learn each one's hidden scoring criteria: completion time, damage taken, accuracy and optional objectives usually drive the medal. There is no mission replay, so keep a manual save before every mission and check your medal the moment the results screen appears, reloading straight away if it is below gold. Play methodically, use cover, aim for headshots to keep accuracy high, and skip unnecessary detours to protect the clock. Some late missions have tight time thresholds, so upgrade your weapons and armor first. Treat this as a slow, reload-heavy playthrough rather than a clean run.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"just-like-paradise","grade":"bronze","name":"Just Like Paradise","description":"Complete Gone Fishing.","guide":"The story's first proper mission, Gone Fishing, opens Chapter 1 in Port Gellhorn and doubles as the game's tutorial. It cannot be failed or missed, so just follow the objectives and the trophy pops at the end. Take the time to get used to the cover, aiming and swimming controls here, because they carry through every later mission. There are no hidden requirements, no real combat to manage and no medal to worry about. If you are also going for Pacifist and Ghost, this is the ideal mission to earn those on, since it is so low-pressure. Then start watching for the Chapter 1 meditation that Positive Mental Attitude needs.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://gta.wiki/w/Achievements_and_Trophies_in_GTA_VI","title":"Achievements and Trophies in Grand Theft Auto VI","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"paradise-lost","grade":"bronze","name":"Paradise Lost","description":"Complete Chapter 1.","guide":"Finish Chapter 1, which is set around Port Gellhorn and ends after the mission Down to Earth. The trophy pops when Chapter 2 actually begins, so if you do not see it right at the final cutscene, do not worry. Before you leave Chapter 1, make sure you have done the missable balcony meditation for Positive Mental Attitude: the morning after Down to Earth, talk to Lucia in the kitchen and choose Accept, then follow her outside to meditate. Keep a manual save at the end of the chapter, since there is no mission replay and you will want a clean Chapter 1 save to fall back on.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"t-s-ass-drug-money","grade":"bronze","name":"T**s Ass Drug Money","description":"Complete Chapter 2.","guide":"Finish Chapter 2, which introduces the drug trade and the fencing loop that funds the rest of the game. The chapter includes Breakfast Run, so expect the Trust trophy to pop along the way. This one awards as Chapter 3 begins, after the Welcome to Vice City sequence, so a short delay is normal. Chapter 2 is where optional missions start appearing in force; do them as they show up because they quietly build toward the 100 optional tasks that Completionist wants. Keep a manual save at the chapter's end, and scan every new vehicle you see with the WAiNK app so the 200-scan requirement never becomes a grind.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"trust","grade":"bronze","name":"Trust","description":"Complete Breakfast Run.","guide":"Complete Breakfast Run, a Chapter 2 story mission early in the Vice City stretch. It is unmissable if you follow the main path, and its only real risk is rushing the final stretch while under fire. Stock up on armor beforehand, take cover during the shootout, and use a decent car for the getaway section. There are no hidden objectives to chase and no medal that matters here, so play it steady. If you are also working on Pacifist or Ghost, save those for an easier mission instead, since this one forces at least some confrontation. The trophy pops right as the mission ends.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"break-the-bank","grade":"bronze","name":"Break the Bank","description":"Complete The Cartel Heist.","guide":"Complete The Cartel Heist in Chapter 3, the story's big set-piece robbery. It runs on the same heist loop you will repeat for bank jobs, so treat it as practice for Mastermind and the 22 bank jobs Completionist needs. Before starting, buy armor, upgrade a fast getaway car, and save manually. The mission walks through the casing, entry and escape phases; if you fail any objective, reload immediately to keep a clean run for Mastermind. Afterward you keep the Dye Pack Jammer, which unlocks fencing marked bills from banks, so finishing this mission is also the key that starts the Millionaire grind.","kind":"story","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":1,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"positive-mental-attitude","grade":"bronze","name":"Positive Mental Attitude","description":"Meditate at every spot across Leonida.","guide":"Meditate at every spot across Leonida, and treat the Chapter 1 one as urgent because it is the only missable trophy in the game. The morning after the Down to Earth mission, talk to Lucia in the kitchen at Jason's house and choose Accept, then follow her to the balcony to meditate; this one does not appear as a normal Meditation Spot on the map, so it is easy to skip, and it locks out forever once you push into Chapter 2. The other spots are marked and can be done anytime in free-roam, and each counts twice if you meditate as both Jason and Lucia. Only 15 of 18 are needed for 100%, but the trophy wants all of them.","kind":"collectible","missable":true,"missableNote":"The Chapter 1 balcony meditation is the point of no return: trigger it the morning after Down to Earth, before starting Chapter 2.","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-all-meditation-spot-locations/","title":"GTA 6 All Meditation Spot Locations","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"lets-go-bowling","grade":"bronze","name":"Let's Go Bowling","description":"Complete all bowling alleys.","guide":"Visit every bowling alley in Leonida and complete their games. The flagship is the Kolt & Associates alley on Ocean Beach, but several others are tucked around Vice City and Port Gellhorn; check the map filter for Activities to find them. Each alley has its own game variant, so set the marker straight, release at full power and adjust for the lane's drift to reach a strike. You do not need perfect scores, just to finish each location. Do them as you pass through each region during the story so you are not driving all over the map at the end.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"leonida-road-trip","grade":"bronze","name":"Leonida Road Trip","description":"Complete all races in Leonida.","guide":"Complete every race in Leonida. Races appear as map icons across the whole state and unlock region by region as you progress, so sweep each area once its icons show up. There are 40 unique races total, and winning 30 of them is what Completionist actually counts, so this trophy sits comfortably on top of that requirement. Bring a fast, upgraded car and learn each course's shortcuts; restarting a race you lose is free and fast. The 13 race challenges with gold medals are tracked separately under Progress, so do not confuse the two. Spread them out and the trophy comes naturally before the endgame.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"wanted-dead-or-alive","grade":"bronze","name":"Wanted: Dead or Alive","description":"Complete all bounty hunter missions.","guide":"Complete every bounty hunter mission. Bounties are posted at sheriff stations and notice boards around Leonida, and each target has a last-known location on the map. Approach quietly where you can: a stealth takedown or a stun keeps the target alive for the higher alive payout and avoids a chase, while killing them still clears the job. Some targets are guarded or will run, so bring a rifle and a fast car in case it turns into a pursuit. Work them region by region as you travel, and check back at each board after story chapters, since new bounties unlock over time.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"king-of-the-strip","grade":"bronze","name":"King of the Strip","description":"Complete all the golf challenges.","guide":"Complete all the golf challenges. Mini-golf courses are scattered around the strip and resort areas, and two of the three locations are what Completionist needs, but this trophy wants every hole at every course cleared. Each challenge asks for under par on the hole, so judge the green's slope before you putt and aim wide of hazards. The swing meter rewards a smooth, near-full stroke rather than a maxed one. Do a course fully in one visit so you do not forget which holes you have cleared, and mark them off as you finish. It is one of the quicker activity sets.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"suns-out-guns-out","grade":"bronze","name":"Suns out, Guns out","description":"Complete all shooting ranges.","guide":"Complete every shooting range challenge. Ranges are found at Ammu-Nation stores and standalone locations across Vice City and the countryside, and Completionist demands gold medals at all 42 of them, so aim for gold on the first pass rather than just finishing. Each round scores accuracy and time: switch targets fast, avoid spraying, and reload between waves. Upgrade a stable pistol and rifle first, since some rounds are tight on the timer. If you are close to gold but miss, replay immediately while the rhythm is fresh. This is one of the more demanding sets, so budget real time for it.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"flipper","grade":"bronze","name":"Flipper","description":"Complete all triathlons.","guide":"Complete every triathlon. Triathlons run swim-bike-run segments, so build your stamina and cardio first by sprinting and swimming regularly, otherwise the final leg will drain you. The events are marked on the map once you reach the region, and each is a set course with checkpoints. Pace the swim, hammer the bike on straightaways, and save a little sprint for the run. You do not need first place everywhere, just to finish each event, so steady beats fast. Do them with a full stamina bar and you will clear the set without much trouble.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"deep-dive","grade":"bronze","name":"Deep Dive","description":"Find all underwater treasure.","guide":"Find every underwater treasure. The map has 33 underwater discovery sites, and all of them are required for Completionist, so this trophy is a strict superset of that. You need scuba gear or a rebreather plus a strong swimmer or submersible to reach the deeper spots, so buy the gear as soon as it is available. Sonar pings help locate crates and wrecks, so watch the mini-map while submerged. Work the coastline and rivers systematically rather than randomly, and mark off each find as you go. Some sites are deep and dark, so bring a flashlight and watch your oxygen.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"air-superiority","grade":"bronze","name":"Air Superiority","description":"Complete all flight school lessons.","guide":"Complete every flight school lesson. The flight school unlocks early and is the fastest way to learn the aircraft handling you will need for Under the Bridge and the VCIA getaway. Each lesson grades takeoff, navigation and landing, so repeat any you score poorly on until it clicks; landings are where most players lose points. Do the school in one sitting while the controls are fresh. Afterward, buy or borrow a nimble plane and practice low, stable flight, because you will reuse those exact skills for the bridge-flying trophy. Gold medals here are not required, just completion.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"gridlock","grade":"bronze","name":"Gridlock","description":"Complete all taxi fares.","guide":"Complete every taxi fare. Flag down or call a taxi and take over the driving, then run fares from the meter. Passengers tip for fast, clean trips, so follow the route and avoid collisions that scare them off. The fares are scattered around Vice City and the suburbs, and the set expands as you reach new districts, so revisit the cab stand after each chapter. It is slow but trivial, perfect to chip away at between story missions. Some fares have time pressure or a nervous passenger, so keep the cab repaired. Completing them all takes patience more than skill.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"firestarter","grade":"bronze","name":"Firestarter","description":"Complete all fire truck missions.","guide":"Complete every fire truck mission. Get behind the wheel of a fire truck, usually parked at stations around Leonida, and respond to the calls that appear once you are in the cab. Each mission asks you to reach a burning scene and put out the flames with the hose before the timer ends, so aim the water at the base of the fire and move quickly. Keep the truck intact, since a wrecked ladder or pump fails the run. New calls unlock as you complete the current ones, so stay in the truck and work through the chain. Do it in one long session.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"paramedic","grade":"bronze","name":"Paramedic","description":"Complete all ambulance missions.","guide":"Complete every ambulance mission. Grab an ambulance, typically at hospitals, and answer the dispatch calls. You will pick up patients under a timer and race them to the hospital while their vitals drop, so drive fast but steady: rough crashes worsen their condition and can fail you. Memorize the shortest routes between pickup points and the ER, and use the siren to split traffic. Chain the calls together without leaving the vehicle, since the set advances one mission at a time. It is a test of clean driving under pressure, not raw speed.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"vigilante","grade":"bronze","name":"Vigilante","description":"Complete all vigilante missions.","guide":"Complete every vigilante mission. These become available in a police or neighborhood-watch vehicle and send you after wanted criminals around the city. Each wave gives you a target to stop, either by disabling their car or taking them out, with a timer running. Use a fast pursuit car and ram the target's vehicle off the road rather than trading bullets. New targets keep appearing as you clear them, so stay in the vehicle and work the full chain. Be careful not to rack up your own wanted level in the process, or you will be fighting on two fronts.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"hoarder","grade":"bronze","name":"Hoarder","description":"Collect all hidden packages.","guide":"Collect every hidden package. Hidden packages are tucked into alleys, rooftops, docks and backrooms across Leonida, and several sit inside story buildings, so sweep each mission area thoroughly while you are there. Use the collectible notifications you turned on in settings, and watch the minimap for the telltale glow. Some are high up and need a ladder or helicopter, so come prepared with a way to climb. Work region by region with a checklist so you do not lose count. A few are in buildings that become inaccessible later, so grab them on the first visit.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"landmark","grade":"bronze","name":"Landmark","description":"Visit all landmarks in Leonida.","guide":"Visit every landmark across Leonida. Landmarks are the named points of interest on the map, from Vice City's neon strip to the swamps and air bases of Mariana County. Simply getting close enough to each one registers it, so drive or fly a route that touches them all. Unfog the map by exploring, since landmarks only reveal themselves once you have visited the area. The game's own map filter can list discovered landmarks, so use it to see what is left. Combine this with the Under the Bridge and Wildlife Photographer runs to make one efficient exploration tour.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"wildlife-photographer","grade":"bronze","name":"Wildlife Photographer","description":"Photograph all wildlife species.","guide":"Photograph every wildlife species across Leonida. Unlike the binocular study that Completionist needs, which is 100 of 255 animals, this wants an actual photo of each species, so pull out the camera and snap everything you see: birds, dogs, cats, deer, gators in the swamp and fish near the shore. Different species live in different biomes, so vary your route between the northern swamps, the countryside and the coast. Approach slowly or use zoom so animals do not spook. Track your shots under Progress and cross-reference a species list so you know exactly what is missing.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"stuntman","grade":"bronze","name":"Stuntman","description":"Complete all stunt jumps.","guide":"Complete every stunt jump. There are 130 stunt jumps marked across Leonida, and Completionist needs 300 stunts overall, so this is the biggest single slice of that. Each jump needs a ramp or ledge, enough speed, and a clean landing, so use a fast sports car or bike and line up straight. The landing is what counts, so clear the landing zone rather than just launching. Marked jumps show on the map once found, and PowerPyx's location guide maps them all. Some require specific vehicles or a running start, so be patient on the finicky ones.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-all-stunt-jump-locations/","title":"GTA 6 All Stunt Jump Locations","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-all-challenges-guide/","title":"GTA 6 All Challenges Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"under-the-bridge","grade":"bronze","name":"Under the Bridge","description":"Fly under all bridges.","guide":"Fly under every bridge in Leonida. There are 202 under-the-bridge stunts, best done in a small, agile plane or helicopter with stable low-speed handling. Fly under each bridge and keep the wings level so you do not clip the supports, which resets the attempt. Start in the flat, open waterways around Vice City, then work the tighter river bridges in the countryside. A slow, high-wing plane makes the narrow ones far easier than a jet. Combine this with the stunt and landmark runs to clear the map in fewer passes.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-all-challenges-guide/","title":"GTA 6 All Challenges Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"sharp-shooter","grade":"bronze","name":"Sharp Shooter","description":"Get a headshot with every weapon.","guide":"Land a headshot with every weapon in the game. The 66 standard-issue weapons split into 53 guns, 9 melee and 4 explosives, and you will find or buy them all as you play; expanded Ammu-Nation stores carry the full inventory. Firearms are easy, just aim high. Melee headshots are the awkward part, so line up the strike on a downed or stunned enemy. Explosives cannot headshot, so they are excluded from the tally despite being in the list. Track your progress in Progress > Weapons and tick off each one as you go.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":5,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"full-garage","grade":"bronze","name":"Full Garage","description":"Own every vehicle type.","guide":"Own one of every vehicle type in the game. There are 277 base-model vehicles across classes like sedans, muscle cars, supercars, trucks, bikes, boats and aircraft, plus 280 standout vehicles at fixed locations. You do not need every model, just each type, so fill your garages and hangar slots with one from every class you encounter. Steal what is on the road and buy or unlock the rest; aircraft and boats need their own storage. Use the WAiNK app to scan and identify vehicles as you collect them, and keep a running list of classes you still need.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"wardrobe","grade":"bronze","name":"Wardrobe","description":"Buy every clothing item.","guide":"Buy every clothing item in the game. Shops are spread across Vice City and the beach towns, and each carries a rotating stock, so revisit stores and check every category: tops, bottoms, shoes, accessories and outfits. Cash is not a real obstacle once you start fencing stolen goods, so buy in bulk whenever you pass a shop. Keep an eye on the style-discovery counter too, since Completionist wants 70 of 79 discovered styles, which overlaps heavily with this. Buy the expensive one-off pieces as soon as they appear rather than waiting until the end.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"tuned-up","grade":"bronze","name":"Tuned Up","description":"Fully upgrade a vehicle.","guide":"Fully upgrade a single vehicle. Take any car you like to a mod shop and buy every available upgrade across performance and body categories: engine, brakes, transmission, suspension, armor and the cosmetic extras. Costs add up fast, so do this once you have a healthy bankroll from fencing. It does not matter which car, so pick one you will actually drive for the races and pursuits. A fully tuned vehicle also makes the Racer, Leonida Road Trip and Survivor trophies noticeably easier, so upgrade early and let the investment pay for itself across the rest of the run.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":5,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"property-mogul","grade":"bronze","name":"Property Mogul","description":"Buy every property.","guide":"Buy every property in the game. Properties range from safehouses and garages to businesses that generate income, and each is a one-time purchase from its sign or the real-estate site. Prices climb steeply, so bank a big reserve first: fencing narcotics, jewelry and marked bills through your contacts is the fastest money. Garages double as vehicle storage, so prioritize those early. Work through the cheapest properties first and reinvest any passive income. Everything is purchasable in free-roam after the story, so nothing here is missable.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"millionaire","grade":"bronze","name":"Millionaire","description":"Earn $10,000,000.","guide":"Earn ten million dollars in total. The fastest route is fencing stolen goods: narcotics and jewelry from gang operations and smash-and-grabs, plus marked bills from bank vaults once you have the Dye Pack Jammer from Chapter 3. A single large bank vault can net over two hundred thousand, and gang operations respawn for repeat looting. Combine active heists with the passive income from businesses you have bought, and do not hoard: spending still counts toward the lifetime-earned total. Keep laundering through your contacts so the money actually registers.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":5,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"socialite","grade":"bronze","name":"Socialite","description":"Reach maximum relationship with every contact.","guide":"Reach maximum relationship with every contact. Contacts include your partner and the cast of fixers and friends you meet through the story and side missions; hang out with them, complete their missions and answer their calls to raise the meter. Each contact has their own activities, so mix in outings like bowling, golf and meals rather than repeating one. Their final missions and loyalty tiers unlock as the relationship climbs, which feeds the Strangers & Freaks progress too. Some contacts are unavailable for stretches of the story but all return in free-roam, so nothing is missable.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":5,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"hacker","grade":"bronze","name":"Hacker","description":"Complete all hacking minigames.","guide":"Complete every hacking minigame. Hacking pops up in story missions, heists and side jobs, usually as a timed circuit or code-cracking puzzle on a phone or terminal. The minigames vary, so learn each pattern: match the highlighted nodes, trace the signal, or brute the code by elimination. The Dye Pack Jammer and Key Cloner are hacking tools you will use to bypass alarms and locks, and each use counts toward the tally. If a hack is time-pressured, plan the route before you start inputting. Repeat any you fail, since they are all freely retryable.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"diver","grade":"bronze","name":"Diver","description":"Complete all salvage missions.","guide":"Complete every salvage mission. Salvage jobs send you to retrieve cargo or wrecks from the water, usually for a fixer who pays per run. You will need the diving gear and a boat or submersible to reach the sites, so gear up first. Each mission marks a salvage point; dive down, grab or cut loose the target, and surface before your air runs out. Watch for the oxygen gauge and any aggressive wildlife near the wrecks. New salvage runs unlock as you complete the previous ones, so chain them together in one coastal session.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"smuggler","grade":"bronze","name":"Smuggler","description":"Complete all smuggling runs.","guide":"Complete every smuggling run. Smuggling means moving contraband between drop points across Leonida while dodging the cops or rival gangs, usually in a specific vehicle. Plan the route before you start so you can avoid checkpoints, and keep the cargo undamaged or the run fails. A fast, handling-focused car helps on the winding backroads, and a plane or boat features in some runs. Heat attracts attention, so drive clean until you are spotted. These unlock progressively as your contacts grow, and each completed run moves you toward the next.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true},{"id":"racer","grade":"bronze","name":"Racer","description":"Win a race in every class.","guide":"Win a race in every vehicle class. Races cover cars, bikes, boats and possibly aircraft, each class with its own events on the map. Enter one race per class and come first; you do not need to win every race in a class, just one apiece. Bring the best vehicle you own for each category and learn the course before committing. For the slower classes, upgrade your entry first, since the AI can be competitive. Check the map's race icons and their class labels so you do not skip a category, and this will overlap neatly with the Leonida Road Trip wins.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"golfer","grade":"bronze","name":"Golfer","description":"Score under par on every hole.","guide":"Score under par on every golf hole. Unlike the mini-golf challenges, this is full-size golf, so it rewards club selection and reading the green. Judge distance and wind before each shot, lay up on long holes, and putt with a light touch on downhill greens. Under par means birdie or better, so aim to reach greens in regulation and sink the putts. Missed putts are where most rounds slip away, so practice the putting meter until it is reliable. Play a full round at each course and retry any hole you bogey rather than finishing the round.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"tennis-pro","grade":"bronze","name":"Tennis Pro","description":"Win a tennis match.","guide":"Win a single tennis match. Find a court, usually at a resort or country club, and challenge an opponent. Position matters more than power: return to the center of the court after every shot and aim for the open side your opponent leaves. Use the timing meter to place powerful serves and angled returns, but do not overhit into the net. Win two sets and the trophy pops. If you lose, rematch immediately while the timing is fresh. It is a short, low-stakes activity, so knock it out the first time you pass a court.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"arm-wrestler","grade":"bronze","name":"Arm Wrestler","description":"Win an arm wrestling match.","guide":"Win an arm wrestling match. Find an arm wrestling table, often in bars, gyms or beach promenades, and accept a challenge. It is a timing minigame: match the on-screen rhythm and tap or hold at the right moment to push your opponent's arm down, saving a burst for when their meter drops. Stamina drains fast, so do not spam inputs, follow the beat instead. Lose and you can immediately challenge again. Different opponents have different rhythms, so if one is too fast, try another venue. It takes a minute once you get the cadence.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"dancer","grade":"bronze","name":"Dancer","description":"Get a perfect score at the club.","guide":"Get a perfect score at the club. Hit the dance floor at a nightclub in Vice City and follow the rhythm prompts that appear on screen. Each prompt asks for a direction or button in time with the beat, and a perfect score means hitting every cue without a miss, so watch the approaching icons and tap on the beat, not early. Use a headset or pay attention to the music's pulse to stay locked in. If you miss a cue, restart the song rather than finishing it. It is one of the quicker activity trophies once you find the timing.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"gambler","grade":"bronze","name":"Gambler","description":"Win at every casino game.","guide":"Win at every casino game. Casinos in Vice City offer poker, blackjack, roulette, slots and more, and you need a win at each. Blackjack is pure odds, so play basic strategy and stand on 17; poker rewards patience and folding bad hands; roulette is best played by spreading small bets on colors or dozens. Slots are luck, so budget a little and spin until you hit. Quit each table the moment you book a win and move on. Track which games you have won so you do not revisit a table you have already cleared.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"pool-shark","grade":"bronze","name":"Pool Shark","description":"Win a game of pool.","guide":"Win a game of pool. Find a pool table, usually in bars and social clubs, and beat an opponent. Aim with the cue line, account for the cut angle, and strike with a smooth half-power stroke so the ball rolls true. Line up your next shot while deciding the current one, and play safe when there is no easy pot. Completionist only needs five of seven pool opponents, but this trophy just wants a single win, so it pops the first time you sink the deciding ball. Miss and you can re-rack and try again.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"domino","grade":"bronze","name":"Domino","description":"Win a game of dominoes.","guide":"Win a game of dominoes. Find a domino table, often in parks or social halls, and play a match. It is a matching game: play tiles whose ends match the open values, and offload your highest tiles early to keep your hand small. Watch what your opponent plays to guess what they hold, and block their doubles when you can. A win counts as soon as you empty your hand or force a block. The AI is beatable with basic strategy, so a match or two is usually enough. Retry freely if you lose.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"angler","grade":"bronze","name":"Angler","description":"Catch every fish species.","guide":"Catch every fish species in Leonida. Fish species are tied to water types, so work the ocean, rivers, swamps and ponds with the right bait and rod. Watch the line tension and reel in bursts, stopping when the fish pulls so the line does not snap. Cal's fishing challenges double as practice and count toward optional tasks, so do them along the way. Rare species live in specific spots, so consult a fishing map for the hard-to-find ones. It is a patience trophy: settle in and work each biome until its species list is empty.","kind":"collectible","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":4,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"hunter","grade":"bronze","name":"Hunter","description":"Complete all hunting challenges.","guide":"Complete every hunting challenge. Hunting runs through Bret Vogel's Target Decks, a 15-part questline that asks you to track and take down specific animals across the swamps and countryside. A clean shot to the head or heart keeps the animal pristine and pays more, so use the unique Killtelligence SM-69 rifle Bret gives you and aim carefully. Tracking markers lead you to each animal, but they spook easily, so approach downwind and use cover. All 15 decks are required for Completionist, making this one of the longer single-thread tasks.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":3,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"mechanic","grade":"bronze","name":"Mechanic","description":"Repair every vehicle type.","guide":"Repair every vehicle type. As you drive each class of vehicle, visit a repair shop or use a repair item to fix it up, registering each type as you go. Most vehicles take visible damage in normal play, so simply driving each class and stopping for repairs after a rough stretch covers most of the list. Track which classes you have repaired and knock out the rest by deliberately damaging and fixing them. It is a passive trophy for the most part, but boats and aircraft are easy to forget, so be intentional about those.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":5,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"courier","grade":"bronze","name":"Courier","description":"Complete all delivery missions.","guide":"Complete every delivery mission. Delivery work comes from contacts like Moses and Randy, who send you to move vehicles or packages between locations across Leonida. Each delivery is a point-to-point drive with a timer or condition, usually keep the cargo intact and get there before the clock runs out. These count as optional tasks too, so they feed Completionist's 100-task requirement. New deliveries unlock as you finish them, so work through each contact's list. Do them when they appear during the story to avoid a long backlog at the end.","kind":"activity","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":2,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-100-completion-checklist-guide/","title":"GTA 6 100% Completion Checklist & Guide","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":false},{"id":"influencer","grade":"bronze","name":"Influencer","description":"Reach maximum followers.","guide":"Reach maximum followers. Followers are tied to your online presence in-game, and they grow as you scan things with the WAiNK app, complete activities and post to your feed. Keep the app active while exploring and scan vehicles, animals and points of interest, since each scan nudges your following up. Trendy, high-profile stunts and rare discoveries give bigger follower bumps, so chase the unusual stuff. The counter lives in your phone's social app, so check it regularly. It accrues slowly, so treat it as a background goal you chip away at all game.","kind":"misc","missable":false,"missableNote":"","roadmapStage":5,"sources":[{"url":"https://www.powerpyx.com/gta-6-grand-theft-auto-vi-trophy-guide-roadmap/","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Roadmap","retrieved":"2026-11-19"},{"url":"https://www.gtabase.com/gta-6/achievements","title":"GTA 6 Trophy Guide & Achievements List","retrieved":"2026-11-19"}],"spoiler":true}];